Z||000002||JSocha||04-23-2001||10:40 AM||||Most search engines have an "Add URL" feature.  Click on those, enter your website address (aka Universe Resource Locator URL) and your site will be spidered by their "bots".<P>Just viewed your SOURCE code for your website, you may want to add more KEYWORDS to get your listing higher.<P>Also, you may want to add this into each web page right after the KEYWORDS and DESCRIPTION right before the "[/head]":<P>"&lt;meta name="ROBOTS" content=all&gt;"<P>This way if you have multiple keywords that are similiar like "Fiero, GT Fiero, SE Fiero, etc." the search engines will accept duplicates on the name Fiero, otherwise, it is considered spamming to them and they will blacklist you.<P>If you need help Lisa, email me at work (jsocha@rugbymfg.com) or home (socha@stellarnet.com).<P>I also have a listing of websites you can go to for information on how Search Engines list your website and rules to consider so not to get "black listed".<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jnjsochasig.jpg">   <P>[This message has been edited by JSocha <P>PS:  No foals yet.  Both mares overdue on top of it!  Excited though!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 04-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||PatrickB||04-23-2001||11:37 AM||||Everything you will need:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.search.com/guides/submit/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.search.com/guides/submit/index.html</A> <P>Tells you how to get your site ready and has tools to submit to all the search engines.||||reg||10
Z||000004||Cameron||04-24-2001||04:21 AM||||In most search engines as previously stated there is an add site/url link on there.  Yahoo has one that is pretty easy to find.  Fill out all the information and away it goes.  If they think it's worthy they add it.  Yahoo for one looks at the applications and decides if it's ok.  Others don't look and you are directly added.  Check out <A HREF="http://www.yahoo.com" TARGET=_blank>Yahoo!</A>, <A HREF="http://www.excite.com" TARGET=_blank>Excite</A>, <A HREF="http://www.lycos.com" TARGET=_blank>Lycos</A>, <A HREF="http://www.altavista.com" TARGET=_blank>Altavista</A>, <A HREF="http://www.google.com" TARGET=_blank>Google</A>, and/or <A HREF="http://www.dmoz.org" TARGET=_blank>Open Directory Project (not sure bout this one)</A>.<P>And yes, there are lots of programs you can use for minimal fees that instantly send applications to add your website to thousands of search engines.  Any of the ways are good.<P>Good luck, and happy hunting.<P>And on a side note:<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>PS: No foals yet. Both mares overdue on top of it! Excited though!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>JSocha, a horse person? cool send me an e-mail when ya get a chance I wanna hear all about it.<P><P>------------------<BR>Cameron<BR> <A HREF="http://Fiero.NetMARC.com" TARGET=_blank>http://Fiero.NetMARC.com</A> ||||reg||1
